   "source": [
    "# 3D-ΔPDF: analysis-only prototype\n\n**This is a synthetic volume, not DISCUS output.** A quantitative 3D-ΔPDF requires a Bragg-subtracted diffuse intensity volume on a corrected, centered Cartesian Q grid; Bragg subtraction, masking, normalization, and voxel interpolation are outside this starter."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "f50d5965",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom discuspdf import delta_pdf_from_diffuse, plot_delta_pdf_slice"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cb767e05",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Construct a synthetic centrosymmetric diffuse intensity\n\nCoordinates below are in physical Q units Å⁻¹."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "a9ab24a2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "n = 64\ndq = 0.15  # Å^-1\nq = (np.arange(n) - n//2) * dq\nqx, qy, qz = np.meshgrid(q, q, q, indexing=\"ij\")\n# An example smooth, nonnegative centrosymmetric feature\ni_diff = np.exp(-((qx-1.1)**2+qy**2+qz**2)/(2*0.35**2))\ni_diff += np.exp(-((qx+1.1)**2+qy**2+qz**2)/(2*0.35**2))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "667bc994",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Transform to a real-space 3D-ΔPDF"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1d063e96",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "delta, r_axes = delta_pdf_from_diffuse(i_diff, (q, q, q))\nax = plot_delta_pdf_slice(delta, r_axes, axis=2)\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "cb9a9962",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Replace synthetic data with your own\n\nFor an HDF5 file, identify the actual dataset paths first. **Do not assume** a universal DISCUS HDF5 layout.\n\n```python\nfrom discuspdf import read_hdf5_volume\nintensity, q_axes = read_hdf5_volume(\n    \"your_diffuse_volume.h5\",\n    intensity_dataset=\"/actual/intensity/path\",\n    q_datasets=(\"/actual/qx/path\", \"/actual/qy/path\", \"/actual/qz/path\"),\n)\nfft = delta_pdf_from_diffuse(intensity, q_axes)\\n",
    "print(fft.diagnostics)\\n",
    "delta, r_axes = fft.real_volume, fft.r_axes\n```\n\nIf the source uses h,k,l reciprocal-lattice coordinates, first map the data to an appropriately sampled Cartesian Q grid using the reciprocal-cell metric."
   ]
  }
